--- reading it
    Cost tracks query x reference cells, not genomes: 1x1 -> NxN multiplies the cells by
    100, so dividing wall time by the number of genomes overstates the growth. Compare
    1x1 -> 1xN (query scaling) with 1x1 -> Nx1 (reference scaling) before attributing
    growth to the shared index. Peak RSS is a per-process high-water mark.

